  {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/smn/SubyearlingFreshwaterResidence",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Beacham, T.D. and Withler, R.E. 2017, Population structure of sea-type and lake-type sockeye salmon and kokanee in the Fraser River and Columbia River drainages, PLOS ONE 12(9):e0183713, which states that sea-type juveniles do not spend a winter in fresh water and thus lack a freshwater annulus."
      }
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
      {
        "@id": "https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0183713"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://w3id.org/smn"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Subyearling migrant"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
      {
        "@id": "https://w3id.org/smn/JuvenileFreshwaterResidenceDuration"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Juvenile freshwater residence of less than one year: juveniles migrate seaward during their first year, without overwintering in fresh water, and therefore carry no freshwater annulus on the scale."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://w3id.org/smn/JuvenileFreshwaterResidenceDurationScheme"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Subyearling freshwater residence"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "The freshwater annulus is the operational test, and it is the reason this axis is cut here rather than at some other duration. Two boundaries are easy to get wrong. The incubation winter spent in the gravel as egg and alevin lays down no annulus and does not count against this value. And this value means no freshwater WINTER, not no freshwater rearing: a subyearling migrant may spend weeks or months in flowing water, sloughs, or the estuary first, which is why it can and does carry a value on the rearing habitat axis. A dataset that keys its equivalent category on residency duration rather than on the annulus is therefore measuring something adjacent, not the same thing, and the two usually but not always agree."
      }
    ]
  },
